Hi Emily and Kylie,

Kylie, sorry my dataset is rather large (~7-10gb), but I am happy to share it if Emily's does not work.

Emily, as a sort of bandaid fix, I forked Cardinal and made a branch of version 2.4.0 with my modified file here https://github.com/gtluu/Cardinal/blob/v2.4.0.9000/R/stats2-spatialShrunkenCentroids.R. Specifically, the lines that were modified were Lines 219-231 and Lines 311-312 from that link.

Some things that I have noticed to keep in mind, the "problematic pixels" that are causing this error cannot be categorized into a class so they are removed from the segmentation map and just appear as a white/blank pixel. There is also the big caveat that while the code functions, I am not completely sure what underlying implications this may have (if any) on the SSC algorithm/other statistical analysis due to this change, though I have not noticed any very obvious ones. So at the moment, this is very much a "use it at your own risk" type of situation.

- Gordon

