Until effective coregistration with optical images is implemented, the only way to select an ROI is from an ion image using selectROI().

This takes the same arguments as the image() method, and returns a logical vector giving the indices of the selected region.

It is up to you to find an appropriate ion image to use, based either on data exploration or known m/z values that correlate with the region of interest. Unfortunately, I can't really help with that part.

