Hi Emily,

you don't need to know an m/z, you can also select regions on unsupervised clustering results e.g. pca, spatialkmeans, spatialshrunkencentroids:

segm_result = spatialShrunkenCentroids(test4, k=2, s=2, r=1)
image(segm_result)
ROI1 <- selectROI(segm_result, mode="region")
ROI2 <- selectROI(segm_result, mode="region")
regions <- makeFactor(ROI1=ROI1, ROI2=ROI2)
test4$region <- regions
pData(test4)

Melanie

